{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "promissory-note-to-jason-brunell-14-september-1837", "page": "2", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/2040/2040_ms155_5_06_001_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "[1]", "href": "/paper-summary/promissory-note-to-jason-brunell-14-september-1837/1"}, {"image": "/2040/2040_ms155_5_06_002_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "[2]", "href": "/paper-summary/promissory-note-to-jason-brunell-14-september-1837/2"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "promissory-note-to-jason-brunell-14-september-1837", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD5", "documentSeriesTitle": "Promissory Note to Jason Brunell, 14 September 1837", "editorialPageNumber": "2", "isPageNumberPresent": false, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/53993456/53993456-0002.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6367572381746960192\"><a href=\"#6367572381746960192\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans3\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/brigham-young\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Brigham Young</a> handwriting ends; first unidentified scribe begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Recd this 3<span class=\"underscore\">rd</span> Day October 1840 on the within fifteen Dollars</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"18155823370288751202\"><a href=\"#18155823370288751202\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans4\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">First unidentified scribe handwriting ends; second unidentified scribe begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Recd this 5th of October 1840 on the within nine Dollars</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5259765217055600185\"><a href=\"#5259765217055600185\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans5\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Second unidentified scribe handwriting ends; <a href=\"/person/newel-kimball-whitney\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Newel K. Whitney</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Recd 23d. July 1841 at <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16712199615938189431\"><a href=\"#16712199615938189431\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc12\" place=\"plc12\" title=\"Nauvoo, Illinois\">Nauvoo</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Nauvoo, Illinois\"><p>Principal gathering place for Saints following expulsion from Missouri. Beginning in 1839, Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints purchased lands in earlier settlement of Commerce and planned settlement of Commerce City, as well as surrounding areas....</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/nauvoo-illinois\">More Info</a></div></div></aside> Ill. One Hundred and four dollars in Goods &amp; cash on the within</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11196808395441549295\"><a href=\"#11196808395441549295\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans6\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/newel-kimball-whitney\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Newel K. Whitney</a> handwriting ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside> 1842 Received on the within Ten dollars</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1568532386410572904\"><a href=\"#1568532386410572904\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans7\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting continues, though written at a later time than the previous line. Text from this point forward written vertically across preceding text.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Received 12 one buggy. per hand.</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12296751648462108415\"><a href=\"#12296751648462108415\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per172\" person=\"per172\" title=\"Jared Carter\">Jared Carter</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Carter, Jared\"><p>14 June 1801–6 July 1849. Born at Killingworth, Middlesex Co., Connecticut. Son of Gideon Carter and Johanna Sims. Moved to Benson, Rutland Co., Vermont, by 1810. Married Lydia Ames, 20 Sept. 1823, at Benson. Moved to Chenango, Broome Co., New York, by Jan...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/jared-carter\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside> <a href=\"/paper-summary/the-book-of-the-law-of-the-lord/91\" class=\"externalLink\">Law of the Lord page 79</a>.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5198462770407593621\"><a href=\"#5198462770407593621\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans5\"><span id=\"documenttrans5\">5</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">The <a href=\"/place/nauvoo-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Nauvoo</a>-era “<a href=\"/paper-summary/the-book-of-the-law-of-the-lord-book-a\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/the-book-of-the-law-of-the-lord-book-a\" poptitle=\"The Book of the Law of the Lord, Book A\">Book of the Law of the Lord</a>” records a tithing payment by <a href=\"/person/jared-carter\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Jared Carter</a> for one buggy valued at eighty dollars. That inscription was crossed out, suggesting that although the buggy may have initially been intended as a tithing payment, it was instead applied to the debt on this promissory note. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/the-book-of-the-law-of-the-lord-book-a/50\" class=\"externalLink\">Book of the Law of the Lord, 79</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside> value eighty dollars. on the within.—</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14638223563290409231\"><a href=\"#14638223563290409231\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans8\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting continues, written still later.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Rceived Feb <span class=\"underscore\">th</span> A. Bond for a Lot west of John Hais in Kimballs additin value. $75.—</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9672460154427996856\"><a href=\"#9672460154427996856\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans9\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting ends; <a href=\"/person/william-clayton\" class=\"referenceInPop\">William Clayton</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Received [on] the within March 30<span class=\"underscore\">th</span>. 1842 one hundred and ninety dollars &amp; fifty four cents.</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2753961434468381417\"><a href=\"#2753961434468381417\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans10\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Handwriting of <a href=\"/person/william-clayton\" class=\"referenceInPop\">William Clayton</a> continues, though written at a later time.</p><hr></div></div></aside>April 11<span class=\"underscore\">th</span>. 1842 Received on the within one hundred and fourteen dollars and thirty five [ce]nts [p. [2]]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3667719711508703461\"><a href=\"#3667719711508703461\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans3\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/brigham-young\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Brigham Young</a> handwriting ends; first unidentified scribe begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Recd this 3<span class=\"superscript\"><span class=\"underscore\">rd</span></span> Day October 1840 on the within fifteen <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Dollars</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6771526089830626676\"><a href=\"#6771526089830626676\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans4\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">First unidentified scribe handwriting ends; second unidentified scribe begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Recd this 5<span class=\"superscript\">th</span> of October 1840 on the within <span class=\"deleted\">sixteen</span> &lt;​nine​&gt; <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Dollars</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4679636265548592474\"><a href=\"#4679636265548592474\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans5\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Second unidentified scribe handwriting ends; <a href=\"/person/newel-kimball-whitney\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Newel K. Whitney</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Rec<span class=\"superscript\">d</span> 23<span class=\"superscript\">d.</span> July 1841 at <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1313926272851389180\"><a href=\"#1313926272851389180\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc12\" place=\"plc12\" title=\"Nauvoo, Illinois\">Nauvoo</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Nauvoo, Illinois\"><p>Principal gathering place for Saints following expulsion from Missouri. Beginning in 1839, Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints purchased lands in earlier settlement of Commerce and planned settlement of Commerce City, as well as surrounding areas....</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/nauvoo-illinois\">More Info</a></div></div></aside> Ill. One Hundred <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and four dollars in Goods &amp; cash on the within</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10607350000949958563\"><a href=\"#10607350000949958563\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans6\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/newel-kimball-whitney\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Newel K. Whitney</a> handwriting ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside> 1842 Received on the within <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Ten dollars</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17881204559596624951\"><a href=\"#17881204559596624951\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans7\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting continues, though written at a later time than the previous line. Text from this point forward written vertically across preceding text.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Received 12 one buggy. per hand.</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1123178577361938991\"><a href=\"#1123178577361938991\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per172\" person=\"per172\" title=\"Jared Carter\">Jared Carte[r]</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Carter, Jared\"><p>14 June 1801–6 July 1849. Born at Killingworth, Middlesex Co., Connecticut. Son of Gideon Carter and Johanna Sims. Moved to Benson, Rutland Co., Vermont, by 1810. Married Lydia Ames, 20 Sept. 1823, at Benson. Moved to Chenango, Broome Co., New York, by Jan...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/jared-carter\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7443686495227788491\"><a href=\"#7443686495227788491\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans4\"><span id=\"documenttrans4\">4</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: Cut-out signature on opposite side of page results in missing text. From this point forward, text is supplied based on context.</p><hr></div></div></aside> <a href=\"/paper-summary/the-book-of-the-law-of-the-lord/91\" class=\"externalLink\">Law of the Lord page 79</a>.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15020514091641253103\"><a href=\"#15020514091641253103\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans5\"><span id=\"documenttrans5\">5</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">The <a href=\"/place/nauvoo-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Nauvoo</a>-era “<a href=\"/paper-summary/the-book-of-the-law-of-the-lord-book-a\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/the-book-of-the-law-of-the-lord-book-a\" poptitle=\"The Book of the Law of the Lord, Book A\">Book of the Law of the Lord</a>” records a tithing payment by <a href=\"/person/jared-carter\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Jared Carter</a> for one buggy valued at eighty dollars. That inscription was crossed out, suggesting that although the buggy may have initially been intended as a tithing payment, it was instead applied to the debt on this promissory note. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/the-book-of-the-law-of-the-lord-book-a/50\" class=\"externalLink\">Book of the Law of the Lord, 79</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside> value <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>eighty d[ol]lars. on the within.—</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17379661132797823131\"><a href=\"#17379661132797823131\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans8\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting continues, written still later.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Rceived Feb <span class=\"superscript\"><span class=\"underscore\">th</span></span> A. Bond for a Lot west <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>of John Hais in Kimballs additin <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>value. $75.—</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11432078276561216909\"><a href=\"#11432078276561216909\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans9\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting ends; <a href=\"/person/william-clayton\" class=\"referenceInPop\">William Clayton</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Received [on] the within March 30<span class=\"superscript\"><span class=\"underscore\">th</span>.</span> 1842 <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>one hundre[d] and ninety dollars &amp; fifty <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>four cents.</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10031305253953305152\"><a href=\"#10031305253953305152\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans10\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Handwriting of <a href=\"/person/william-clayton\" class=\"referenceInPop\">William Clayton</a> continues, though written at a later time.</p><hr></div></div></aside>April 11<span class=\"superscript\"><span class=\"underscore\">th</span>.</span> [184]2 Received on the within <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>one hundr[ed] and fourteen dollars and <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>thirty five [ce]nts [p. [2]]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/2040/2040_ms155_5_06_002_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/2040/2040_ms155_5_06_002_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/2040/2040_ms155_5_06_002.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/2040/2040_ms155_5_06_002_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/2040/2040_ms155_5_06_002.xml", "classification": "Documents", "publishe